    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0022" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg15"/>

                <head>No. 10.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Braida to Mr. Uhl.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San Juan
                                del Norte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-07"><hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 21.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to transmit herewith a report of
                    consular agent, Mr. Seat, at Bluefields. The Nicaraguan troops arrived here on
                    their way <pb facs="0023" n="16" xml:id="pg16"/> to the interior, on board of
                    Her Majesty’s ship <hi rendition="#italic">Cleopatra</hi>, yesterday
                    morning.</p>
                <p>I furthermore inclose, in translation, a copy of the provisional treaty concluded
                    between Gen. C. A. Lacayo and Captain Howe, commander of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cleopatra</hi>, countersigned by Her British Majesty’s
                    consul, Mr. H. F. Bingham, who also returned on the man-of-war from
                    Bluefields.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. C. Braida</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d10-a1.xml" xpointer="d10-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d10-a2.xml" xpointer="d10-a2"/>
